# SHA-256 pins for every artifact the kev image downloads (issue #6).
#
# Sourced by BOTH:
#   - docker/kev/Dockerfile   (build-time: torch wheel, kev.serve tarball)
#   - docker/kev/entrypoint.sh (first-boot: HF weights; boot aborts on mismatch)
#
# Provenance (recorded 2026-10-13, batch-1 fix):
#   ADAPTER_SHA256 / BASE_MODEL_SHA256 — sha256sum of the local serving
#     copies at ~/workspace/kev-serve/models/ (byte-identical to the
#     HuggingFace blobs; sizes match the entrypoint's old size checks:
#     43338624 / 1746942600 bytes). Safetensors files are never
#     modified after download, so the local copies ARE the pristine
#     upstream bytes.
#   HEAD_PT_SHA256 — sha256sum of a FRESHLY re-downloaded pristine copy
#     of jaredpalmer/kev-0.8b head.pt (2,103,999 bytes, matches the old
#     size check). The local serving copy was patched (meta.base
#     rewritten to the local base dir) and MUST NOT be pinned here:
#     verification happens at download time, BEFORE the entrypoint's
#     patch step rewrites the file.
#   TORCH_WHEEL_SHA256 — hash fragment from the official PyTorch PEP 503
#     simple index (https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu/torch/), the
#     same digest pip would verify in --require-hashes mode.
#   KEV_TARBALL_SHA256 — sha256sum of the GitHub codeload tarball for
#     the pinned KEV_COMMIT (deterministic per commit).
#
# If an upstream artifact is ever re-pinned, update the value here —
# this file is the single source of truth.

ADAPTER_SHA256=72813c8de3ce3a60fcdd0ee6f1448780e689d572f99f2f79a3f947c345597e62
BASE_MODEL_SHA256=9c17d06a4992596d7d2609cb880c4692733b9928e5b38048a0650ce6033a4605
HEAD_PT_SHA256=f400bd12802b2b105ae45d6b03774a158a3db4fccff42413734ddca2e5c920b6
TORCH_WHEEL_SHA256=cb9a8ba8137ab24e36bf1742cb79a1294bd374db570f09fc15a5e1318160db4e
KEV_TARBALL_SHA256=16cc5f2e72e862870bcdd8501a34b3c43e8afb224815fb16ea09c7e2005c3f48
